    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining our offensive strategy. His matchup against Bieber carries an elite efficiency score of 73.66, bolstered significantly by a favorable park factor and a 19% boost from the opposing starter's xERA of 5.25. While we are tracking the pending lineup, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** serves as our anchor, complemented by **Kyle Tucker** (66.24) and **Andy Pages** (64.71). Both **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** benefit from wind-aided conditions in their tilt against Gasser, providing a higher ceiling for power production in a game where the platoon advantages are effectively neutralized. **Luis Robert Jr.** also remains a critical start (64.28); despite an elite hold catcher impacting his steal potential, the favorable platoon split against Alvarez keeps him as a top-tier rotation component.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was the exclusion of **Jackson Merrill** (50.99) from the active roster. While **Jackson Merrill** presented a compelling case due to his strong recency and platoon edge, he was ultimately edged out by the superior efficiency and matchup profiles of our utility and outfield slots. The primary warning for today remains the high volume of \"Lineup Pending\" designations; while we have modeled expectations for players like **Gunnar Henderson** (60.09) and **Jacob Wilson** (61.95), any unexpected shifts in the batting order could deflate these efficiency scores, particularly for **Gunnar Henderson**, whose value is sensitive to his #1 slotting. Furthermore, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces a stern test against Cole; while his 56.43 score is tempered by the pitcher\u2019s skill, his historical BvP elite status (41 PA) provides a necessary insurance policy against an otherwise challenging matchup.",
